WEBVTT

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:08.980
Ball!

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.570
Ball!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.700
Ball!

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.880
I won't hit it!

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.670
I won't be fooled by those pitches.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.410
I still need to let our fourth batter, Tashiro, up here.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.500
You're talkative.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.840
Let me say this: Kaido's manual doesn't say to walk someone...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.470
in fear of allowing a run or two at the beginning of the game.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.760
Strike!

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.060
A-A challenge?

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.190
I thought I was being underestimated for a while there.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.660
Well, it's fine if you underestimate me.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.780
I'll let you know what you're risking with that carefree attitude!

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:07.590
Strike!

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:09.580
Batter out!

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.740
<i>A-A forkball?</i>

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.050
<i>A-A forkball?</i>

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.170
<i>That Ichihara...</i>

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.760
<i>He wasn't able to throw a forkball before!</i>

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.480
Batting fourth: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.410
Strike!

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.000
<i>I see.</i>

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.980
<i>This guy's pitches are a lot stronger than they looked when I was on the bench.</i>

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.380
<i>I could hit it easily, but it would likely go to the infield.</i>

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.630
<i>But...</i>

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.350
<i>if we get the first run off of Kaido, it'll give us confidence for the rest of the game.</i>

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.340
<i>In order to give Shigeno an easier time on the mound,</i>

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.260
<i>I can't let go of this chance to knock in the first run!</i>

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.110
<i>A trick play!</i>

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.070
Run, Tashiro!

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.110
Out!

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.890
Amazing...

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.330
Shit, and I knew it too!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.880
<i>But, we have confidence.</i>

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:05.960
<i>We have the absolute confidence that our development over the year won't lose to yours.</i>

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.750
<i>Now I get it.</i>

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:14.010
<i>So that unpleasant attitude of yours was to show off your confidence, eh?</i>

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.200
S-Sorry.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.000
I ruined a good chance.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.280
Don't feel down, Tashiro.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.700
If you start feeling down now, you'll lose the possibility of seeing the goddess of victory in the sky.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.810
I-In the sky?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.700
It's just an example.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.170
An example.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.620
Bottom of the first inning: leading off for Kaido Academy...

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.710
Batting first: center fielder, Kusano-kun.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:46.930
Play!

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.310
<i>It's rare...</i>

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:02.590
<i>that my throat feels this dry from excitement.</i>

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.900
<i>Here it comes, Kaido!</i>

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.960
Strike!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.630
F-Fast.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:19.540
It rose another level today...

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.630
Shigeno-kun's fastball.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.760
Ball!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.800
<i>As expected from Kaido's first batter;
the way he watches the ball is so different.</i>

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:41.620
<i>He's completely driven into a corner,</i>

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.560
<i>yet he's calmly observing when the ball will go slightly off-course.</i>

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.190
<i>Careful as always, Kusano,</i>

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:52.610
<i>or is it just that you can't hit it even if you swing!?</i>

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.970
Foul!

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:03.830
Well, I never thought you'd be an easy person to strike out.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.080
Foul!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.410
Foul!

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:15.090
Now that I think about it, when was the last time we've seen Kusano get struck out?

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.310
I don't remember.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.270
<i>You still haven't hit the core of it!</i>

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.190
Ball!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.740
Four balls!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.400
Kaido got someone on base.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:32.320
It can't be helped when they're so persistent.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.080
Batting second: second baseman, Tokashiki-kun.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:40.040
Play!

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.040
<i>He's trying to steal a base.</i>

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.970
<i>I know you don't like it much,</i>

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.390
<i>but make sure you use your pickoff move on him.</i>

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.810
Strike!

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.560
Safe!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.690
T-Time!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:09.280
He got away so easily because you didn't try to pick him off!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.950
This is Kaido, remember!? Kaido!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.870
Did you think you could hold them at bay with such a crude strategy!?

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.560
If he was someone I could stop with pickoff attempts, I would've stopped him.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:19.090
What?

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:23.030
If I struggle around with that, he'll run anyway.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:27.150
If we make this game against Kaido's veteran players a strategy battle,

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.550
they'll just keep tricking us.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.470
I won't get caught up in their pace.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.230
We'll go with our own pace.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.720
Just as long as they don't get home, it's fine!

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:43.690
Play!

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.790
<i>As long as I strike them out, it doesn't matter!</i>

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:52.940
Crap!

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.160
S-Safe!

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.380
That idiot... He did it again.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.470
S-Sorry.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.220
Batting third: third baseman, Yakushiji-kun.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.110
Foul!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.940
He's already in a pinch, that Shigeno-kun.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.800
Yeah.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:40.800
A year ago, nobody was able to do anything against his pitches.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:48.170
But now, nobody has even swung and hit air.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:49.720
Foul!

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.080
During the year, even though Shigeno-kun has been improving,

00:08:53.800 --> 00:09:00.390
with the 200 games and spring selection process that Kaido went through,

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.070
the difference in experience is showing, whether he likes it or not.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:06.310
Foul!

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.230
Kaido really is amazing.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.830
Nobody has even swung and hit air with Honda's pitches.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.100
If it's about swinging and hitting nothing but air, I wasn't either.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:20.480
Until the final, decisive one Honda-kun threw, that is.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:32.370
<i>With the condition of my foot in mind, I was planning on taking it easy at first, but...</i>

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:36.760
<i>if I do that, there's no way I'll be able to match up against Kaido!</i>

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.470
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.890
He did it!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.800
Amazing!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.970
See? This is Honda-kun.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:53.180
<i>As usual, your pitches get even stronger when you're challenged.</i>

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:57.360
Batting fourth: catcher, Sato-kun.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.290
Play!

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.900
<i>It's been a long time since we've had a duel face-to-face, Toshi.</i>

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:16.420
<i>We have confidence.</i>

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:22.420
<i>Then I'll just have to smash through that confidence!</i>

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:26.350
<i>S...</i>

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.590
Squeeze!?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.650
W-What!?

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:40.340
Safe!

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.290
F-First!

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.200
Out!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.020
K-Kaido used a squeeze?

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:49.200
And Toshi-kun was the one to use it!

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.760
T-They've gotten tough.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:58.600
That means that those on Kaido's bench are more afraid of Shigeno-kun than we thought.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:03.510
It was likely... Egashira's orders, however.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.360
It's turning out more like how you planned.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.640
<i>Got it? With a runner on and no outs, steal a base,</i>

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:18.330
<i>and if it gets to a one out and a runner on third, score a run with a squeeze.</i>

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:23.290
<i>The guys who have lost to them so far did so because they tried to directly match up against him.</i>

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.240
<i>Those who fight with power will only be opposed with more power.</i>

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:33.110
<i>Steal away their confidence with the precision of the baseball manual!</i>

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.930
Well, we'll patiently let it stew,

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:40.980
until both their bodies and minds are a mess, ever so slowly.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:44.660
Strike!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:45.770
Batter out!

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:47.090
Three outs! Change!

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:53.560
Top of the second inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.560
Batting fifth: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.380
All right!

00:11:58.380 --> 00:11:59.280
It's payback time!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.000
Out!

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:13.460
Strike! Batter out!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.070
Three outs! Change!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.660
That happened in a blink of an eye.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.290
Let Honda get a break...

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:25.610
Oh, crap!

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.940
Huh, Shimizu-san, you didn't bring a poncho?

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:30.970
Nope...

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.100
Then you can borrow this.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.770
As expected, you're a life-saver, Komori.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.920
I didn't look at the weather report at all, so...

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.490
But I wonder if it'll be okay.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.560
It'd be fine if it ended in the seventh inning, but...

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.940
if the rain gets stronger,

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.070
the game might be cancelled.

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.910
Cancel the game...

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.050
Ball!

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.110
Four balls!

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.600
This inning they have a runner on with no outs too.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.770
Batting seventh: right fielder, Yaoita-kun.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.590
<i>Shigeno, you...</i>

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:23.520
<i>You said you wouldn't get caught up in their pace,</i>

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:25.520
<i>but we'll be done for at this rate!</i>

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:32.750
<i>If they score a second run against us, it'll get even harder!</i>

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:37.520
Out!

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:41.220
It's the same attack pattern they used in the first inning.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.900
Coach, isn't there something they can do?

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.200
Trust them. Trust Nogoro-kun and the others.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.760
Batting eighth: shortstop, Izumi-kun.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:02.000
<i>This isn't a squeeze again, is it?</i>

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.650
<i>I won't let you do it easily this time!</i>

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.080
Ball!

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.860
<i>Did he read it?</i>

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.340
Ball!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.770
<i>He's not going to do it?</i>

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.550
<i>I can't waste any more pitches like this.</i>

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.630
<i>Now he's doing it!?</i>

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:34.090
Tashiro, catch it!

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:39.140
This is a free fansub.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:39.140
Not for sale or rent.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.670
Strike!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.690
Out!

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.160
T-They did it!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.200
Amazing!

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.380
Two outs! Two outs!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.830
A-A ball in the dirt!?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.240
You can't bunt those...

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.960
Did he pull that out of the blue?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:23.500
<i>To use something like that to get out of the squeeze...</i>

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:28.490
<i>The way you break past things is interesting, as usual, Goro-kun.</i>

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:31.470
Strike!

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:32.850
Batter out!

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.850
Three outs! Change!

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:40.120
Strike!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.320
This isn't good.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.590
The rest of the order can't do a thing.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:48.900
Are things okay like this, Senpai?

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:53.100
Shigeno-senpai and Tashiro-senpai are another matter,

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:58.020
but everyone else can't hit the ball, and just goes up to the plate and spaces out.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.060
It's not giving us any chances.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.970
What?

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:05.820
Who are you saying is spacing out!?

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.910
I'm doing the best I can too, hey!

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.440
Just because you were able to get a hit...!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.910
Hey, quit it!

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.410
Do you have any good ideas, Shimizu-kun?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.910
Not really.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.680
Just that if we're going to strikeout so much,

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.830
sacrifice bunts or whatever would be better.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.790
Bunt!?

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.000
Are you an idiot?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.630
With Kaido's defense as it is, that won't get us on base!

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:39.010
No, that might be better than doing nothing.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:45.060
The ground is getting slippier with the rain.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.400
These conditions aren't easy for Kaido either.

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:51.060
Strike! Batter out!

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:54.740
That's not bad:

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.070
a mutual disadvantage.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:59.670
Batting ninth: left fielder, Noguchi-kun.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:01.060
Noguchi!

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:12.910
Play!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.090
<i>Are they planning to squeeze too?</i>

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:21.710
Out!

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.850
Well, it might not go well at first.

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:29.060
I see. A bunting strategy?

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.030
At least they put some thought into it.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.740
Batting first: right fielder, Shimizu-kun.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.600
Play!

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:43.770
<i>A bunt again?</i>

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.050
Strike!

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:52.390
If you can't hit it, did you think you'd have a chance if you bunted?

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:53.460
Look!

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:55.580
They have us completely figured out!

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:59.580
With that defense of theirs, bunting is pointless!

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:04.480
Besides, that guy doesn't need to do that when he can hit...

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.340
A fake bunt!?

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.560
Fair!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.570
A-All right!

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:17.650
Run, Taiga!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.330
Safe!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.400
He did it! A double!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.510
All right!

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:25.910
Good job, Taiga!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:35.550
<i>I get it! You planned to fool Kaido like this from the start!</i>

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.670
I see.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:42.530
It seems there are others besides Shigeno who can play baseball on that team.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.470
<i>Nice ball!</i>

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.620
<i>You're a fourth year, right?</i>

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:04.970
<i>Y-Yes!</i>

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.490
<i>You throw well for a fourth year.</i>

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:12.080
<i>I'm sure you'll be a great player.</i>

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:14.820
<i>Really?</i>

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.860
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:25.130
All right! Taiga's on base!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.470
We're counting on you, Uchiyama!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.690
Do whatever! Just get it to Shigeno!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.830
Geez, just like in the first inning, he let another runner on base.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:37.890
That first batter is pretty good.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.120
Play!

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:45.330
<i>Goro-kun is next.</i>

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.860
<i>I definitely can't let this batter get on base.</i>

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.570
H-Hey, Taiga's...

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:56.260
Isn't that lead a little too wide!?

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:57.010
Yeah...

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.670
S-Safe!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.020
That was close...

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.940
What are you doing!?

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:10.660
We're on with two outs! We don't have the option of taking such huge risks!

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:16.610
<i>"We don't have the option of taking such huge risks"?</i>

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.920
<i>We have no other option but to take huge risks!</i>

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:27.710
He's running!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.790
That idiot!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.460
Does he plan to steal a base on Toshi-kun?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:31.780
Ball!

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:35.790
Safe!

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.260
I know he throws well!

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:44.200
<i>So that's what this is about.</i>

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.410
Ball!

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:51.120
That guy...

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.710
Does he think he can steal third base on Kaido's battery?

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:57.820
We finally have a good opportunity!

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.770
No, Taiga's goal isn't to steal a base.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:13.810
Ball!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.860
Ball three!

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.130
Look!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.820
The pitcher wasn't throwing balls before,

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:27.500
but with Taiga provoking him to the edge,
it's disrupting his rhythm!

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:31.600
The bunting strategy was good.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:35.550
He speaks rudely, but he's truly trying to do something about this!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.740
Shimizu-kun...

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:55.220
He's getting a little cocky.

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:55.990
Yep.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:59.990
Maybe it's about time he got disciplined.

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:13.610
H-He did it!

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:14.640
It's loose!

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:18.120
<i>I was waiting for them to miss!</i>

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:24.660
What!?

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:28.700
Out!

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.420
Hey, you,

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:36.340
your senses aren't bad,

00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:40.290
but you should be a little more humble against us.

00:22:45.910 --> 00:22:50.450
Was... he throwing to the backup in center on purpose?

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:52.940
What's up with that trick play?

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:02.250
<i>Now I get it.</i>

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:05.430
<i>It's still far away from home plate.</i>

00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:43.270
Kaido continues with its baseball manual to the bitter end.

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:45.990
The manual won't work on me anymore!

00:24:45.990 --> 00:24:48.730
What's with Toshiya and that easygoing manner?

00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:52.090
It can't be... Did he find a weakness in my pitching?

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:53.920
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.920 --> 00:24:55.550
Toshiya's Secret Plan.

00:24:55.550 --> 00:24:57.840
Run to the stage of your dreams!
